  "translationRepairs": [
    ["s0116","idiomatic","Martial and Martial-Fang Generals; the Huaihai and Mountain-Forest Commandants; and staff officers of the various bureaus of the Far-Pacifying, Loyalty-Establishing, Stalwart, Northern-Soothing, Far-Soothing, Glory-Raising, Wave-Quelling, and Light-Chariot headquarters.","Might and Martial-Fang Generals; the Huaihai and Mountain-Forest Commandants; and staff officers of the various bureaus of the Far-Pacifying, Loyalty-Establishing, Stalwart, Northern-Soothing, Far-Soothing, Glory-Raising, Wave-Quelling, and Light-Chariot headquarters.","s0116 lists 威、武牙將軍 as two titles (parallel to 曠野、橫野將軍); 威 is distinct from 武, so replacing the collapsed “Martial and Martial-Fang” with “Might and Martial-Fang” restores the correct first title without other changes.","high","applied"],
    ["s0116","literal","Martial and Martial-Fang Generals; Huaihai and Mountain-Forest Commandants; staff officers of the various bureaus of the Far-Pacifying, Loyalty-Establishing, Stalwart, Northern-Soothing, Far-Soothing, Glory-Raising, Wave-Quelling, and Light-Chariot headquarters.","Might and Martial-Fang Generals; Huaihai and Mountain-Forest Commandants; staff officers of the various bureaus of the Far-Pacifying, Loyalty-Establishing, Stalwart, Northern-Soothing, Far-Soothing, Glory-Raising, Wave-Quelling, and Light-Chariot headquarters.","The same 威、武牙 pair opens the literal sentence; rendering 威 as “Martial” conflates it with 武 in 武牙, and “Might and Martial-Fang Generals” correctly separates the two titles.","high","applied"]
  ],
